WwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2025-10-23T16:28:55Z","updated_at":"2025-10-24T10:40:02Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4.latest, 4.5, 4.5.1\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - i5 13600kf - rtx 4070\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe bounding box (orange in the screens) is broken with collision shapes, it does not encompass them.\n\nImages from MRP:\n<img width=\"1755\" height=\"1167\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ad1146e4-2df5-475c-811a-e73d27cced2d\" />\n\n<img width=\"1577\" height=\"523\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/dd780f14-9a6c-4186-9946-8d130c90dc65\" />\n\n<img width=\"1465\" height=\"1127\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/aa1f8e9d-7a63-4b69-9284-49d3b28c1ac7\" />\n\nDifferent project:\n\n<img width=\"1052\" height=\"984\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1619e67b-d0a7-4dcc-a4c2-5a461f7ba765\" />\n\nAs you can see in the images, the height (y axis) is entirely ignored. The rest seemes to take into account only the centers of the shapes but when you check the \"Different project\" above you can see it's not entirely true, if I move around the shapes sometimes the bounding box disappears entirely or does not take into account some of the shapes - below you can see how it doesn't really take the entire shape into account, if I move the shape to the (0, 0, 0) local to the parent then the AABB disappears entirely.\n\n<img width=\"966\" height=\"946\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d34ee3f6-530f-4f0f-9fae-68b06d6c400d\" />\n\n<img width=\"884\" height=\"835\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a95ff31c-1e67-46a3-baf3-268ba9dba66a\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add a Node3D to your main scene.\n2. Add couple collision shapes to it with a box shape.\n3. Click on the parent Node3D created in 1.\n4. Observe the orange bounding box not including the shapes entirely.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[AabbWrong.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23102472/AabbWrong.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111958/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111958/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}